──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : the always-on footer (web `<footer role="status" aria-live="polite">`) with the left group
                (Connection · divider · Live telemetry) and the right group (Background work · Active vehicle ·
                divider · Help · divider · Version) — every region of StatusBar.tsx + its 6 segment files.
• Connection  : web `useApiHealth` → ok/degraded/offline/unknown, each pairing a tone (emerald/amber/rose/muted)
                with an SF Symbol + dot (color is never the sole encoder), the "API" short label, the latency
                chip (hidden when offline/unknown), and the "· Offline" suffix. Opens system-status.
• Live        : web `useLiveConnection` → connected/reconnecting/disconnected/unknown, spinning glyph while
                reconnecting (Reduce-Motion-aware), the "Live" label + the periodic last-message age
                (ageSecondsLabel ported: s/m/h). Opens the live signal explorer.
• Vehicle     : web `useSelectedVehicle` + `useVehicleState` → hidden (0 cars) / static chip (1) / popover
                switcher (2+); the `display_name || vin || "Vehicle {id}" || "No vehicle"` fallback; the
                "{battery}% · {range} {unit}" metrics chip (convertDistanceFromSI ported, m→km/mi + round).
• Background  : web `useBackgroundJobs` → hidden when idle, else a spinner + the "{count} tasks" summary opening
                a jobs popover (export/mutation/custom icons, "Running" heading, per-job label + detail).
• Help        : web `HelpSegment` → keyboard-shortcuts / take-a-tour / report-bug ghost buttons, each routed to
                a bound-source intent (the web window-event dispatches).
• Version     : web `VersionSegment` → version + git SHA (dev sentinel hidden), update / unseen-changelog dots,
                and the About-this-build sheet (web `Modal`) with the provenance list (app version, commit, helm
                chart, Go runtime, platform os/arch join, server uptime — uptimeLabel ported), the update banner,
                and the changelog / release-notes / close actions.
• Prefs       : web `useStatusBarPrefs` (enabled → renders nothing; iconOnly) + `useNarrowViewport`
                → `iconOnly = compact || prefs.iconOnly || isNarrow`, all on the input snapshot.
• States      : loading (skeleton chrome) / empty (all-unknown → friendly, never a blank box; the always-present
                Help+Version remain) / error (QueryError peer + retry) / data, PLUS the orthogonal stale + offline
                chips (freshness chip + one-shot stale rising-edge auto-refresh) — the full P4 states contract.
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (StatusBarStrings, table "StatusBar"); 55 keys, a perfect 1:1 match
                between StatusBar.strings and the StatusBarCopy catalog (.all). Zero English literals in Swift
                beyond the web-default fallbacks. Web `{{name}}` i18next interpolations → printf positional.
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted exactly once with surface slug "StatusBar".
• a11y        : VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (connection, live, vehicle switcher + each option,
                background popover, 3 help buttons, version, retry); the footer carries the `status` role/landmark;
                Dynamic Type via Font.TS roles; Reduce-Motion-aware spinners + skeleton shimmer.
• Architecture: pure Adapter/Projection/Copy (Sendable, SwiftUI-free, unit-tested) → Model (P1/S8 source seam +
                P1/S11 telemetry seam + P1/S10 facade, @Observable @MainActor) → Views/Segments/Version/States
                (P1/S9 tokens + shared P4 components TSButton/TSSkeleton; no direct library imports, no networking).

